{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-159589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{(x+h)^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{(x+h)^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2h)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y-h+2)^{3}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{h\\to 0}[\\frac{1}{h}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+h+2)^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(y+2)^{3}})]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)={2}^{x+2y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={2}^{x+2y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)={2}^{x+h+2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+2h+2y}-{2}^{x+2yy}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}+{2}^{x+2y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{xh+2y}+{2}^{x+2y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{xh+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{2}^{x+h+2y}-{2}^{x+2y}}{h})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y-h)}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-yh}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-yh}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{h\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)={3}^{xy},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={3}^{xy},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)={3}^{x(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y-h)}+{3}^{xy}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xy+h}-{3}^{xy}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xy-h}+{3}^{xy}}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{xyh}-{3}^{xy}}{h})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{3}^{x(y+h)}-{3}^{xy}}{h})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-h+3y)+\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(xh+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"] ["math" "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{h\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+h+3y)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+3y)}{h})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ given that $f(x,y)=xy+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot 1+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}"] ["math" "x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y"] ["math" "xy+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}"] ["math" "y+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y"] ["math" "y+\\frac{2x}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{2x+3y}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x+3y}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x}\\cdot {e}^{3y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{3}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{3y})+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 3{e}^{3y}+{x}^{2}\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{2x+3y}+2x{y}^{3}"] ["math" "3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"] ["math" "3{e}^{2x+3y}+6x{y}^{2}"] ["math" "6{e}^{2x+3y}+6x{y}^{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{e}^{2x+3y}+3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\cdot (2x)+y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y"] ["math" "2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+x"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-35709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-8{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-16y"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-16y"] ["math" "y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ given that $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot (1)-y\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy,$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(0,\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\pi  \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\pi -1"] ["math" "1-\\pi "] ["math" "1-{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "\\pi +1"] ["math" "{\\pi }^{2}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\pi -1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1+4 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot (1)-x\\cdot (4{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-4x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,1)} & =4\\cdot {2}^{2}-4\\cdot 2\\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =16-8 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-2y\\sqrt{x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,e).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-2y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})-2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-2y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,e)} & =3\\cdot {1}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\frac{e}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =3-e\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bfa07d7e8e9bd2f54ce8367d28161cedf0532fadd238e5e37089ea1c8d04126"} {"question" "q-159597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042597/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9f2bd1e5820ef30e2966e0b6a368692000043a825cb5bcdc1f1a6f03f2ff15"} {"question" "q-159597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" 